  "worked_solution": "The rate at which the speed $V(t)$ of the ship changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum cruising speed and the current speed. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-V),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum cruising speed of the ship, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=90\\text{\u00a0km/h},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k(90-V).\n$$",
